From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-theme-bootstrap: data-page on the root URL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

data-page on <body> was built from ctx.request_path only. When LuCI is
opened by its root URL, which is also where the login redirects to,
the request path is empty and data-page was blank, so the rules of the
theme for a given page (for example the phone layout of the status
overview tables in mobile.css) did not apply until the page was opened
again by its own URL. ctx.path, the resolved route, is used when the
request path is empty.

The same change is in LuCI master.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Uo9XQuT7u6ShTYdi2S3Anq
---
 ucode/template/themes/bootstrap/header.ut | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ucode/template/themes/bootstrap/header.ut b/ucode/template/themes/bootstrap/header.ut
index 3486a412..a7bbf298 100644
--- a/ucode/template/themes/bootstrap/header.ut
+++ b/ucode/template/themes/bootstrap/header.ut
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 		<script src="{{ resource }}/cbi.js"></script>
 	</head>
 
-	<body class="lang_{{ dispatcher.lang }} {{ entityencode(striptags(node?.title ?? ''), true) }}" data-page="{{ entityencode(join('-', ctx.request_path), true) }}">
+	<body class="lang_{{ dispatcher.lang }} {{ entityencode(striptags(node?.title ?? ''), true) }}" data-page="{{ entityencode(join('-', length(ctx.request_path) ? ctx.request_path : ctx.path), true) }}">
 		{% if (!blank_page): %}
 		<header>
 			<a class="brand" href="/">{{ striptags(boardinfo.hostname ?? '?') }}</a>
-- 
